1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,276
Welcome to Unit Three of Algebra Two,
where we go deeper into quadratics. We

2
00:00:05,276 --> 00:00:08,192
start with the three forms of a quadratic.

3
00:00:09,333 --> 00:00:13,621
Standard form is y equals a x squared plus
b x plus c.

4
00:00:14,071 --> 00:00:16,503
It shows the y intercept, c, right away.

5
00:00:17,633 --> 00:00:23,415
Vertex form is y equals a times the
quantity x minus h, squared, plus k.

6
00:00:23,865 --> 00:00:26,105
It shows the vertex, h comma k.

7
00:00:27,233 --> 00:00:33,580
Factored form is y equals a times the
quantity x minus r, times the quantity x

8
00:00:33,580 --> 00:00:34,231
minus s.

9
00:00:34,681 --> 00:00:36,985
It shows the x intercepts, r and s.

10
00:00:38,133 --> 00:00:40,949
The same parabola can be written all three
ways.

11
00:00:41,399 --> 00:00:48,027
y equals x squared minus two x minus three
is the standard form. Factored, it's x

12
00:00:48,027 --> 00:00:54,409
minus three times x plus one. In vertex
form, it's x minus one, squared, minus

13
00:00:54,409 --> 00:00:54,818
four.

14
00:00:55,967 --> 00:01:01,382
Use standard form for the y intercept,
vertex form for the maximum or minimum,

15
00:01:01,382 --> 00:01:03,604
and factored form for the zeros.

16
00:01:04,054 --> 00:01:09,666
The axis of symmetry is halfway between
the zeros: one is halfway between negative

17
00:01:09,666 --> 00:01:10,625
one and three.

18
00:01:11,767 --> 00:01:17,840
Your turn. Write y equals the quantity x
minus two, times the quantity x minus six,

19
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:20,620
in standard form, and find its vertex.

20
00:01:21,070 --> 00:01:22,606
Pause the video and try it.

21
00:01:23,056 --> 00:01:29,134
Standard form: x squared minus eight x
plus twelve. The vertex is at x equals

22
00:01:29,134 --> 00:01:31,739
four, and y equals negative four.

23
00:01:32,866 --> 00:01:37,671
In this lesson, we'll convert standard
form to vertex form by completing the

24
00:01:37,671 --> 00:01:38,114
square.

25
00:01:39,233 --> 00:01:43,883
Write y equals x squared plus eight x plus
ten in vertex form.

26
00:01:44,333 --> 00:01:50,061
Half of eight is four, and four squared is
sixteen. Add and subtract sixteen: x

27
00:01:50,061 --> 00:01:54,339
squared plus eight x plus sixteen, minus
sixteen, plus ten.

28
00:01:54,789 --> 00:01:57,221
That's x plus four, squared, minus six.

29
00:01:58,366 --> 00:02:04,055
When a isn't one, there's one more step.
Take y equals two x squared minus twelve x

30
00:02:04,055 --> 00:02:04,809
plus seven.

31
00:02:05,259 --> 00:02:11,165
First factor two out of the x terms: two
times the quantity x squared minus six x,

32
00:02:11,165 --> 00:02:11,957
plus seven.

33
00:02:13,099 --> 00:02:19,441
Inside, add and subtract nine: two times
the quantity x squared minus six x plus

34
00:02:19,441 --> 00:02:21,739
nine, minus nine, plus seven.

35
00:02:22,189 --> 00:02:28,544
The minus nine is inside, so it's really
minus eighteen outside. So y equals two

36
00:02:28,544 --> 00:02:31,960
times x minus three, squared, minus
eleven.

37
00:02:33,099 --> 00:02:38,539
The vertex is three comma negative eleven,
and since a is positive, it's a minimum.

38
00:02:39,666 --> 00:02:45,597
Check with negative b over two a: twelve
over four is three. And two times nine,

39
00:02:45,597 --> 00:02:50,119
minus thirty-six, plus seven, is negative
eleven. It matches.

40
00:02:51,266 --> 00:02:57,197
Your turn. Write y equals x squared minus
ten x plus twenty-one in vertex form.

41
00:02:57,647 --> 00:02:59,183
Pause the video and try it.

42
00:02:59,633 --> 00:03:05,739
Add and subtract twenty-five: x minus
five, squared, minus four. The vertex is

43
00:03:05,739 --> 00:03:07,697
five comma negative four.

44
00:03:08,833 --> 00:03:14,928
In this lesson, we'll solve inequalities
like x squared minus x minus six is less

45
00:03:14,928 --> 00:03:15,681
than zero.

46
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:23,380
First, solve the equation. x squared minus
x minus six factors as x minus three,

47
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:24,778
times x plus two.

48
00:03:25,228 --> 00:03:30,315
So the zeros are three and negative two.
They split the number line into three

49
00:03:30,315 --> 00:03:30,967
intervals.

50
00:03:32,100 --> 00:03:37,840
Test a point in each interval. At x equals
negative three, the expression is six:

51
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:38,478
positive.

52
00:03:38,928 --> 00:03:44,091
At zero, it's negative six: negative. At
four, it's six: positive. So the

53
00:03:44,091 --> 00:03:47,910
expression is negative between negative
two and three.

54
00:03:49,033 --> 00:03:54,134
The graph shows the same thing. The
parabola is below the x axis between its

55
00:03:54,134 --> 00:03:54,537
zeros.

56
00:03:54,987 --> 00:04:00,878
So x squared minus x minus six is less
than zero when negative two is less than

57
00:04:00,878 --> 00:04:02,966
x, which is less than three.

58
00:04:04,100 --> 00:04:09,581
For greater than or equal to zero, we want
where the parabola is on or above the

59
00:04:09,581 --> 00:04:09,924
axis.

60
00:04:10,374 --> 00:04:15,899
That's x less than or equal to negative
two, or x greater than or equal to three.

61
00:04:17,033 --> 00:04:22,196
If a parabola opening up has no real
zeros, it's always above the axis.

62
00:04:22,646 --> 00:04:28,416
So x squared plus one is greater than zero
for every x, and x squared plus one is

63
00:04:28,416 --> 00:04:30,624
less than zero has no solution.

64
00:04:31,766 --> 00:04:36,822
Your turn. Solve x squared minus four x is
less than or equal to zero.

65
00:04:37,272 --> 00:04:38,808
Pause the video and try it.

66
00:04:39,258 --> 00:04:45,423
x times the quantity x minus four: zeros
at zero and four. The parabola is below

67
00:04:45,423 --> 00:04:50,586
the axis between them, so zero is at most
x, which is at most four.

68
00:04:51,733 --> 00:04:56,307
What happens when a line meets a parabola?
In this lesson, we'll solve

69
00:04:56,307 --> 00:04:57,941
linear-quadratic systems.

70
00:04:59,066 --> 00:05:03,717
A line can cross a parabola twice, touch
it once, or miss it entirely.

71
00:05:04,167 --> 00:05:07,666
So the system can have two, one, or no
real solutions.

72
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:13,472
Use substitution. Set the two expressions
for y equal to each other.

73
00:05:13,922 --> 00:05:16,268
That gives a quadratic equation in x.

74
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:22,157
Solve y equals x squared minus one, and y
equals x plus one.

75
00:05:22,607 --> 00:05:29,509
x squared minus one equals x plus one, so
x squared minus x minus two equals zero.

76
00:05:29,509 --> 00:05:33,380
That factors as x minus two, times x plus
one.

77
00:05:33,830 --> 00:05:39,615
So x equals two or negative one. The
points are two comma three, and negative

78
00:05:39,615 --> 00:05:40,742
one comma zero.

79
00:05:41,866 --> 00:05:46,581
Now try y equals x squared, and y equals
two x minus one.

80
00:05:47,031 --> 00:05:53,391
x squared minus two x plus one equals
zero, which is x minus one, squared. Only

81
00:05:53,391 --> 00:05:58,786
x equals one: the line is tangent to the
parabola at one comma one.

82
00:05:59,933 --> 00:06:04,605
The discriminant of the combined equation
tells the story without solving.

83
00:06:05,055 --> 00:06:09,514
Positive: two points. Zero: tangent.
Negative: no intersection.

84
00:06:10,633 --> 00:06:15,817
Your turn. Solve y equals x squared plus
two, and y equals three x.

85
00:06:16,267 --> 00:06:17,803
Pause the video and try it.

86
00:06:18,253 --> 00:06:24,305
x squared minus three x plus two equals
zero, so x equals one or two. The points

87
00:06:24,305 --> 00:06:27,256
are one comma three, and two comma six.

88
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:33,813
In this last lesson of Unit Three, we'll
use quadratics to model real situations

89
00:06:33,813 --> 00:06:35,504
and find the best values.

90
00:06:36,633 --> 00:06:42,133
A store sells two hundred mugs a month at
ten dollars. For each dollar the price

91
00:06:42,133 --> 00:06:44,057
goes up, it sells ten fewer.

92
00:06:44,507 --> 00:06:50,444
With x price increases, revenue is R
equals the quantity ten plus x, times the

93
00:06:50,444 --> 00:06:52,955
quantity two hundred minus ten x.

94
00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:59,263
Expand: R equals two thousand plus one
hundred x minus ten x squared.

95
00:06:59,713 --> 00:07:05,295
The vertex is at x equals one hundred over
twenty, which is five. So the best price

96
00:07:05,295 --> 00:07:10,273
is fifteen dollars, for revenue of two
thousand two hundred fifty dollars.

97
00:07:11,400 --> 00:07:16,350
When data points follow a curved pattern,
a quadratic regression finds the

98
00:07:16,350 --> 00:07:17,821
best-fitting parabola.

99
00:07:18,271 --> 00:07:24,501
A calculator gives a, b and c. The closer
r squared is to one, the better the fit.

100
00:07:25,633 --> 00:07:31,670
A ball is kicked from the ground at twenty
meters per second. Its height is h equals

101
00:07:31,670 --> 00:07:35,191
negative four point nine t squared plus
twenty t.

102
00:07:35,641 --> 00:07:41,036
It peaks at t equals twenty over nine
point eight, about two point zero four

103
00:07:41,036 --> 00:07:44,089
seconds, at about twenty point four
meters.

104
00:07:45,233 --> 00:07:47,793
Always interpret the answer in context.

105
00:07:48,243 --> 00:07:53,500
Negative times, or selling a negative
number of mugs, don't make sense, so throw

106
00:07:53,500 --> 00:07:54,814
those solutions out.

107
00:07:55,933 --> 00:08:01,896
Your turn. Revenue is R equals negative
five x squared plus one hundred x. At what

108
00:08:01,896 --> 00:08:04,659
x is revenue greatest, and what is it?

109
00:08:05,109 --> 00:08:06,645
Pause the video and try it.

110
00:08:07,095 --> 00:08:10,017
x equals ten, and R equals five hundred.

111
